        {
          "id": 2540819573,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It did start a Windows and macOS build when I rebased it:\n\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/pipelines/1849883902\n\nIs it something different in the compiler used in the Brew based macOS build than the other build?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-03T10:15:37.467Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-03T10:15:37.467Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 388150638,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20062,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2542159698,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "GitLab's macOS hosted runners are currently only available for users with [premium and ultimate subscriptions](https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/runners/hosted_runners/macos/). When someone initially opens a merge request, the pipeline is run in their namespace (in this case giovanni.musto/wireshark), and the macOS job won't run unless they have a premium or ultimate subscription. When one of the core developers rebases the MR, the pipeline gets run in the wireshark/wireshark namespace and under our subscription which has access to the macOS runners.\n\nThe Windows runners are slightly different since we self-host those and they're private to the wireshark/wireshark namespace, but the end result is the same.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1788825804",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-03T19:07:21.243Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-03T19:07:21.243Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 388150638,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20062,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2542186094,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Right, though in this case apparently the offending code compiled without warning with AppleClang 16.0.0 but warned about the comma with AppleClang 14.0.3\n\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/jobs/10231040838\n\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/jobs/10235657662",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
